The source scene contains 346 elements and 208 text elements. The Decision System generates and validates a deterministic, source-faithful static SVG review surface. The editable `.excalidraw` file remains authoritative. This source has no embedded animation ordering, so the interface does not claim an animated version.

## Trust boundaries

| Boundary | Trusted input | Prohibited shortcut |
|---|---|---|
| Authoring | scoped branch and canonical project context | direct production change |
| Pull request | repository code and unprivileged CI token | PR secrets or `pull_request_target` execution |
| Main | passing required checks and explicit owner approval | force push or check bypass |
| Promotion | tested archive, expected SHA-256, approved environment | rebuilding differently for production |
| Runtime | Cloudflare secrets and least-privilege deployment token | credentials in source or artifacts |
| Evidence | hashes, command results, review state | request bodies, PII, tokens, or secret values |

## Implemented in the repository

- least-privilege workflow definitions with top-level `permissions: {}`;
- full-length, reviewed Action pins recorded in `security/approved-actions.yml`;
- separate policy, quality, security, and browser gates;
- deterministic build packaging and SHA-256 verification before promotion;
- separate manual preview, staging, production, and post-deploy workflows;
- production branch check, environment boundary, and single-flight concurrency;
- contact-route validation, request caps, timeout handling, redacted logs, bot controls, and headers;
- canonical standards, runbooks, exception records, and machine-readable policy.

## Requires human activation outside the repository

These controls are **not active merely because their files exist**:

- protect `main` with a GitHub ruleset;
- select the required check names after their first successful run;
- create preview, staging, and production environments;
- configure environment reviewers, deployment branches, and secrets;
- create separate least-privilege Cloudflare tokens;
- configure Cloudflare preview behavior, WAF/rate limiting, alerts, and rollback access;
- enable GitHub secret scanning, push protection, and Dependabot settings.

Beacon currently has one human operator. Independent two-person approval cannot be claimed until a second accountable reviewer is added.

## Failure model

Fail closed when a required gate, artifact digest, approval, credential, or production verification is missing. A failed deployment never authorizes an automatic second deployment. The operator follows the rollback runbook, records the incident, and re-enters the normal pull-request path for a fix.

The repository-level implementation evidence, exact commands, results, and unresolved external controls are recorded in `secure-cicd-implementation-report.md`.
